{
  "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
  "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Why don't you raise the level of the podium a little so we can hear you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The jurors who convicted Mr. House of first degree murder heard that semen stains on the victim's clothing matched Mr. House. They didn't hear the DNA evidence which showed that not to be the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The jurors who convicted Mr. House heard that bloodstains on Mr. House's blue jeans matched the blood belonging to the victim. They didn't hear the assistant chief medical examiner for the State of Tennessee testify that the source of those bloodstains was a sample taken during Ms. Muncey's autopsy, nor did they hear --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: On that point -- on that one point, do you contend that the district court was clearly erroneous?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that all of this stuff would -- would have made a better case for the defendant here. But once the case has been tried and both sides have put on all the evidence they have, we have a -- a much different test, and -- and that is whether any reasonable juror could have found him guilty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Trial counsel had in his possession -- or his expert certainly had in his possession the photograph that showed an entire tube of blood missing. Therefore, he had evidence that there was something wrong with the blood. Trial counsel was actually concerned about this blood. He filed a pretrial motion to suppress this blood evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KISSINGER: We -- we are going to also make the Brady claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: How was -- how was that? I thought you'd go on to say how that -- how was it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SMITH: Agent Bigbee specifically testified that the enzyme was present."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But -- but isn't there also evidence that the spillage in the Styrofoam container seemed to be inadequate to account for all of the blood that was missing from the vial?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Smith",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SMITH: Well, I do think you're wrong, Your Honor, because I -- I think that if you look in the record, there are at least four witnesses who indicated that they saw the blood. One was Special Agent Scott."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Ms. Smith, could -- could you go on to some of the other elements that are contested here? In particular, I'm interested in -- in Mr. Muncey's confession. What -- what do you -- what do you say about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Smith",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SMITH: Your Honor, I -- I think of all the evidence presented below, I think that the confession evidence is -- is perhaps the least reliable in terms of -- of the Schlup analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But wasn't the district court incorrect in that? Because as I understand it, there was evidence from one of the two witnesses who put in the confession evidence that she had gone to the sheriff's department to -- to tell them about the confession and had simply gotten a runaround and finally left."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Well, it did have corroboration. Wasn't there a -- a wound on the victim that was consistent with -- with the confession?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kissinger",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KISSINGER: Very quickly. Dr. Blake's testimony was not, in fact, discredited. Counsel for respondent says that -- places great significance on -- on Dr. Blake's interpretation of the initials inc as standing for incomplete penetration, and that -- correctly that should have been construed as inconclusive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kissinger",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KISSINGER: And that's correct, Your Honor. In trial, he used -- he said that inc stands for incomplete, and then Agent Bigbee at trial proceeded to use incomplete and inconclusive interchangeably just as Dr. Blake did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Page 282 of the joint appendix, he says inconclusive is what the inc stands for. Dr. Blake testified it is incomplete penetration, which I haven't the foggiest idea what that means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In fact, it made two specific credibility findings in this case when it found Mr. House's testimony to be incredible and the testimony of Lora Muncey to be credible."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, in fact, there was -- the murder scene was dry, just as petitioner has informed the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Daughter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The daughter's testimony was that she did not hear any sign of a struggle when she got up immediately after her mother left the home."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Scalia asked was there, in fact, other evidence of -- of rape. Wasn't there, in fact, bruises found on her thighs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Tennessee",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State of Tennessee contended that Mr. House was out murdering Carolyn Muncey, and yet the daughter who was outside of the home within 50 yards of where this murder occurred heard absolutely nothing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Pathologist",
      "case_id": "2005-04-8990",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ed1f7875fa46e77cca277934dfe34b655b069bc75de861a94b8914adaad1730",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ed1f7875fa4-0003-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the pathologist testified, admitted on cross examination, that the scratches on Ms. Muncey's thighs were more likely attributable to her being dragged through the brush and her body being hidden which, incidentally, is an act which Mr. Muncey confessed to doing."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
